  "headline": "Hogs near $56 as pork cutout slips; export sales due 7:30",
  "lead": "December hogs settled at $56.03 while the national cash hog price sat at $43.25. That gap is about $12.78 a hundredweight, and futures buyers are paying well over what packers paid on the kill.",
  "teaser": "Futures hogs sit near $56 while cash hogs trade near $43, with export sales due this morning.",
  "one_number": {
    "value": "462,000",
    "unit": "hogs killed Wednesday, USDA estimate",
    "context": "That is 33,000 fewer than a week ago and 25,293 fewer than a year ago, a lighter kill on the day."
  },
  "sections": [
